## 75. Finite words, actual sources and observation interfaces

A source is a nonempty free ordered tree generated by the two leaves $\alpha,\beta$ and the ordered operation $\langle s,t\rangle$, with a single preparation $p=(a,b)$ in oriented $\mathbb R^3$. Its interpretation and substitution are

$$
E_p(\alpha)=a,\quad E_p(\beta)=b,\quad E_p(\langle s,t\rangle)=E_p(s)\times E_p(t),\qquad
\rho(\alpha)=\beta,\quad\rho(\beta)=\langle\beta,\alpha\rangle.
$$

The substitution preserves every ordered node and the same preparation is used throughout $x_j=E_p(\rho^jt)$; write $q_j=\|x_j\|_2$. The original observer performs exactly three Reads of $x_0,x_1,x_2$, with one destructive substitution between adjacent Reads, then Stop. Targets are all finite $j\geq3$ in that same frame, with unweighted $\sup_{j\geq3}\|\widehat x_j-x_j\|_2\leq E$. Proof constructions using rotations, source generation, orthogonalization or different preparations do not give the observer those actions. Write $\varphi=(1+\sqrt5)/2$. Fibonacci numbers use $F_0=0,F_1=1,F_{i+2}=F_i+F_{i+1}$, and $0^0=1$. The preparation symbol $p$ is locally replaced by a precision integer in the finite-word sections; these are distinct typed objects, and §77's cross vector $K$ is distinct from the accuracy integer $K\geq1$.

The parameter domain is |a|,|b|<=L, Delta=|a|^2|b|^2-(a dot b)^2>=d0, q0,q1,q2<=H, with L,H>0 and 0<d0<L^4. In a plateau q0,q1,q2<=1. Zero-label histories are included; a zero unit label may have nonzero x0. Degenerate preparations are included in the unconditional algebra, although excluded by d0>0 in this domain.

